------\n# Public API\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef scan_for_secrets(self, text: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Return a list of findings for every secret detected in *text*.\n\n    BUG_70: Only plaintext patterns are checked.  Base64-encoded\n    segments are never decoded and re-scanned, so an encoded\n    ``AKIA...`` key or ``ghp_`` token slips through undetected.\n    \"\"\"\n    self.findings = []\n    self._scan_plaintext(text)\n    # BUG_70: base64 segments are not decoded — encoded secrets are missed\n    return list(self.findings)\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Internal helpers\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _scan_plaintext(self, text: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Match each pattern against *text* and record findings.\"\"\"\n    for pattern_type, regex in self.patterns.items():\n        for m in regex.finditer(text):\n            self.findings.append(\n                {\"pattern_type\": pattern_type, \"match\": m.group()}\n            )\n\ndef _try_decode_base64(self, segment: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"Attempt to base64-\n\ndecode *segment*.  Return decoded text or None.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        decoded = base64.b64decode(segment, validate=True).decode(\"utf-8\")\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n    return decoded\n```\n\nThe method needs to iterate through base64 segments found in the text, attempt to decode each one, and then re-scan the decoded content for secrets. After processing all findings, it should notify through the alerts module before returning the results.\n\n```python\n    def scan_for_secrets(self, text: str) -> list[dict[str\n```\n\n, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Return a list of findings for every secret detected in *text*.\n\n        BUG_70: Only plaintext patterns are checked.  Base64-encoded\n        segments are never decoded and re-scanned, so an encoded\n        ``AKIA...`` key or ``ghp_`` token slips through undetected.\n        \"\"\"\n        from orgops import alerts\n        self.findings = []\n        self._scan_plaintext(text)\n        # Decode base64 segments and re-scan for secrets\n        for match in _BASE64_RE.finditer(text):\n            segment = match.group()\n            decoded = self._try_decode_base64(segment)\n            if decoded:\n                self._scan_plaintext(decoded)\n        # Call orgops.alerts.notify for each finding\n        for finding in self.findings:\n            alerts.notify(finding)\n        return list(self.findings)\n\nThe implementation now handles base64-encoded segments by iterating through matches, attempting to decode each one, and rescanning decoded content for secrets. The docstring documents the original issue, and the fix adds the base64 detection loop plus the orgops.alerts notification call for each finding. The indentation needs to be correct—8 spaces for the method body. The fix adds a loop that iterates through base64 matches found by `_BASE64_RE.finditer(text)`, attempts to decode each segment, and rescans any successfully decoded content for secrets. This addresses the bug where encoded credentials slip through undetected.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2771,"cache_read_input_tokens":5829,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2771},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb5ded28-10fd-4dd2-87d5-b05831c68a72","uuid":"10fd0383-9e49-47f0-a0bd-608432ddcc9a"}
